<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hyosung T&amp;C '96 net profit falls.</title>
<headline>Hyosung T&amp;C '96 net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	     (billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)			     937  vs	  1,516</p>
<p>    Net				    7.55  vs	  12.22</p>
<p>    Pre-tax				9.84  vs	  16.05</p>
<p>    Turnover			 1,140.00  vs	 980.00</p>
<p>Dividend</p>
<p>    (pct, par 5,000 won) in cash    2.0  vs	   11.0</p>
<p>				in stock    2.0  vs	   none</p>
<p>NOTE - Hyosung T&amp;C, formerly known as Tong Yang Nylon Co, is a specialised maker of nylon and tirecord. It said its 1996 share capital was unchanged at 8.06 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
